From 89fafd933079afe651616691b09bfe0547e4dd2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 21:17:18 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 287/378] Unified: the "in effect up to here" line, short tool
 panels, picks in words
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- History: a blue line under the step where a part currently ends. Drag it
  up to any earlier step (new steps go in there), back to the bottom or
  double-click it to bring all steps back; one undo step each. Steps below
  the line are greyed, slanted and say "not in effect" (Gui/Tree.cpp). The
  word for the body's Tip is never shown. Right-click: "Insert Here" (also
  on a sketch) and "Bring All Steps Back".
- Tool panels show their few important fields (at most three: e.g. a pad's
  length and "reverse", how it ends only when unusual); the rest is under
  "Details", remembered per tool. Pad, pocket, revolve, groove, hole,
  fillet, chamfer, shell, draft, mirror, patterns and the sketch's size.
- Picks in words instead of internal names: "Pad: top face", "Hole ⌀6:
  inner face", "Pad: vertical edge ×4" — from the step that made the
  element, its role there and the kind of geometry, the same ones counted
  together. In the status bar (under the cursor and picked), as the title
  of the bar next to the picks and in the lists of fillet/chamfer panels.
- "Also the edges in the same direction" no longer picks the seam of a
  hole's wall.

Tests: FreeCADCmd -t TestHistoryLine / TestSelectionWords / TestTaskPanels
/ TestWording.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
